DATA
====

Applies to all data in this repository:

- the sampled TEI letters (data/input/bracket_sample/), the extracted bracketed sequences and their metadata
  (data/input/brackets_sample.json, data/input/brackets_sample.xlsx,
  data/input/corresp-metadata_sample.json, data/sampling/brackets_statistics.xlsx)
- the gold-standard annotations (data/references/)
- the letter excerpts quoted in the prompt templates (data/prompts/)
- the stored LLM output (data/output/)
- the evaluation results and figures (evaluation/results/, evaluation/comparisons/,
  evaluation/aggregated_results.json, evaluation/aggregated_results.xlsx, evaluation/language_scores.xlsx)

This data is licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International License
(CC BY-NC 4.0). To view a copy of this license, visit https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/.

You are free to share and adapt this material for non-commercial purposes, provided you give appropriate
credit and indicate if changes were made.

Source of the letters: "Hammer-Purgstall Briefedition", https://gams.uni-graz.at/context:hpe, version 2024-12-01
(Zentrum für Wissenschaftsgeschichte, University of Graz; project lead Martina Scholger), licensed under
CC BY-NC 4.0, based on Walter Höflechner, "Joseph von Hammer-Purgstall. Briefe". Changes made here: a sample of 90 letters; bracketed sequences extracted
from them; editorial interventions encoded by hand in TEI (gold standard); LLM output and its evaluation.

This sample is drawn from a larger historical correspondence corpus that is not itself part of this
repository. Rights to publish are limited to the sample used here.

THIRD-PARTY FILES
=================

- resources/schema/tei_all.rng: TEI P5 schema (TEI Consortium), available under CC BY and BSD-2-Clause
  (see the licence note in the file)
- resources/tools/jing-RELEASE220.jar: Jing RELAX NG validator (Thai Open Source Software Center Ltd),
  BSD-3-Clause; licence text in resources/tools/jing-COPYING.txt
